Original commit body from 67ca957:

Django URL pattern detection (path, re_path, url) uses function calls,
not decorators, so it cannot be migrated to YAML patterns. The
deprecation warning was misleading since there's no YAML-based
replacement for call-based routing patterns.

Changes:
- Remove _deprecated_route_warnings_emitted tracking set
- Remove _emit_route_deprecation_warning() function
- Remove unused 'warnings' import
- Update docstring to clarify Django detection is NOT deprecated
- Remove TestDjangoRouteDetectionDeprecation test class

The Django URL pattern detection remains in place as it's necessary
for call-based frameworks. See ADR-0003 usage-context-patterns
extension for the principled solution to handle call-based patterns
via YAML in the future.
